DTSTAMP:20260705T040629Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260707T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260707T153000
SUMMARY:Trail Ride to see the Big Boy Train
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Bicycle Club (LBC) Meetup\n**Join Your friends from 
 Rails to Trails and the LBC for a trail ride to see the Big Boy Train when
  it arrives for a 45 minute whistle stop in Lebanon\, Pa. We will leave th
 e famous Root Beer Barrel parking lot in Cornwall at 11am. We will ride th
 e Lebanon Valley trail north to the city of Lebanon.**\n**Biking allows us
  to bypass traffic and parking restriction. At the park 250N 8th Street\, 
 the city is hosting a community heritage festival from 10:00 AM to 2:00 PM
  with food vendors\, live music\, and historical presentations right by th
 e tracks. The train will make a 45 minute stop from 12:30pm to 1:15pm.**\n
 ***Union Pacific's famed [Big Boy No. 4014](https://www.up.com/about-us/hi
 story/steam/big-boy-4014)\, the world's largest operating steam locomotive
 \, will [journey to the East Coast](https://www.up.com/news/heritage/big-b
 oy-northeast-tour-dates-260428) this summer for the first time as part of 
 a historic coast-to-coast tour to celebrate America's 250th anniversary. T
 he tour includes a Fourth of July celebration in Philadelphia\, major disp
 lay events in eight cities and more than 50 whistle-stops in 10 states\, i
 ncluding stops for the first time in Indiana\, Ohio\, New York and Pennsyl
 vania.***\n***In addition to the public display days\, rail fans can see t
 his historic machine in action at over four dozen whistle-stops\, generall
 y 15- to 30- minutes long.***\n***This eastern leg will conclude the Big B
 oy's Coast-to-Coast 2026 tour. Earlier this spring\, the Big Boy visited C
 alifornia with a stop at the [Central Pacific's Milepost Zero in Sacrament
 o](https://www.up.com/news/heritage/big-boy-kicks-off-America250-260410) w
 here eastward construction of the transcontinental railroad began.***\n**H
 elmets are mandatory. No ear buds. Please bring water and a basic repair k
 it (spare tube\, tire levers\, pump/CO2 inflator).To eliminate passing aro
 und a pen and paper waiver\, we require RSVP below to join this ride. Your
  RSVP is your agreement to abide by the club's Code of Conduct \, Rules of
  the Road \, and Ride Waiver**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/lancaster-bicycle-club/events/3155087
 12/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260702T011818Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260702T011818Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
